Back the update_rate claim with the datasheet, and note the P900 mismatch

The draft said 30 Hz "tops out near 15 Hz" from general knowledge. The
Teledyne P900 datasheet says "up to 15 Hz" for every variant in the
series, so the claim now cites a source rather than an impression.

Checking the datasheet turned up more than the rate. The shipped SDF uses
512 beams with a 130 degree field of view: 512 is the P900-90's beam
count and 130 degrees is the P900-130's field of view. No shipping
variant has that combination. Vertical extent and maximum range differ
too. None of this was measured, so it goes in as an observation with
that stated plainly -- a maintainer editing this file would want the
whole list in one place even though only update_rate has numbers behind
it.

make_submittable.py skips submit/README.md in the relative-link check.
That file is an index read inside this repository, where relative links
are correct; it is not pasted into an issue.
